InlineMessage
@atlaskit/inline-message

Props (7)
  appearance     IconAppearance | undefined
  Set the icon to be used before the title. Options are: connectivity, confirmation, info, warning, and error.
  children       string | number | boolean | React.ReactElement<any, string | React.JSXElementConstructor<any>> | It…
  The elements to be displayed by the popup.
  iconLabel      string | undefined
  Text to be used as the label for the button icon. You must use this to provide information for people who use assistive technology when there is no title and/or secondaryText.
  placement      PopupPlacement | undefined
  The placement to be passed to the popup. Determines where around the text the dialog is displayed.
  secondaryText  string | number | boolean | React.ReactElement<any, string | React.JSXElementConstructor<any>> | It…
  Text to display second.
  spacing        IconSpacing | undefined
  The spacing of the underlying icon button. Options are: spacious and compact.
  title          string | number | boolean | React.ReactElement<any, string | React.JSXElementConstructor<any>> | It…
  Text to display first, bolded for emphasis.

Examples (1):

Example 1
  tsx                                                                                               
  import InlineMessage from '@atlaskit/inline-message/inline-message';                              
  const Examples = (): React.JSX.Element => (                                                       
    <>                                                                                              
      <InlineMessage                                                                                
        title="Success"                                                                             
        secondaryText="Your changes have been saved successfully."                                  
        appearance="confirmation"                                                                   
      />                                                                                            
      <InlineMessage                                                                                
        title="Warning"                                                                             
        secondaryText="This action cannot be undone."                                               
        appearance="warning"                                                                        
      />                                                                                            
      <InlineMessage                                                                                
        title="Error"                                                                               
        secondaryText="Something went wrong. Please try again."                                     
        appearance="error"                                                                          
      />                                                                                            
    </>                                                                                             
  );                                                                                                
  export default Examples;                                                                          

